# The Mastra tree this repository is developed and measured against.
#
# Two independent pins, because the two routes answer different questions.
#
# DIST is the published package. It grounds the compiler: @mastra/core ships its own
# sourcemaps with `sourcesContent`, so `bootstrap-mastra.sh --dist` recovers the ORIGINAL
# TypeScript of the workflow engine (~11.8k lines across default.ts, execution-engine.ts,
# workflow.ts and handlers/) without cloning a monorepo. That is the artefact a user of this
# engine actually runs against, so it is the right thing to compile for.
#
# REPO is the git checkout. It is needed only for conformance — running Mastra's own workflow
# test suite under both engines — because the published package does not ship tests.
#
# A figure measured against one is not comparable with one measured against the other, and
# neither is comparable with a figure measured against a linked libpetri tree.
MASTRA_DIST_VERSION=1.67.0
